From 642c6283e2e495b235f6b44d713a7c56bdf067c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Mattias=20Walstr=C3=B6m?= <lazzer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:55:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hostapd: Do not limit the BSSID mask to 40 bits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Organization: Wires

hostapd_validate_bssid_configuration() refused to start when the
generated BSSID mask needed more than 40 bits, i.e., when the configured
per-BSS BSSIDs differ from the radio address in the most significant
octet. That is the case when the BSSIDs are not derived from the OUI of
the radio address but assigned from a separate, externally managed
range.

Drop the limit. The mask generation below handles the wider masks
without change, and the driver is left to reject address combinations it
cannot support.

Signed-off-by: Mattias Walström <lazzer@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index fbcd0218b..3dec46250 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -961,12 +961,6 @@ static int hostapd_validate_bssid_configuration(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	if (bits < j)
 		bits = j;
 
-	if (bits > 40) {
-		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "Too many bits in the BSSID mask (%u)",
-			   bits);
-		return -1;
-	}
-
 	os_memset(mask, 0xff, ETH_ALEN);
 	j = bits / 8;
 	for (i = 5; i > 5 - j; i--)
-- 
